  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BBC Media Action. Bridges.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BBC Media Action&#x2019;s overall objective is that people in developing countries take positive actions to adapt to climate change and build resilience to climate-related natural hazards as a result of improved WCIS. Their target groups are the most vulnerable to climate change in Nepal, Bangladesh and Kenya and those responsible for the production and dissemination of weather and climate-related information. BBC Media Action expect at least 10.5 million people will engage with the project&#x2019;s media outputs. The project is expected to have a positive impact on gender equality, as analysis of women&#x2019;s particular needs in relation to WCIS will feed into all project strategies.

Specific objectives are:
1: To increase knowledge and skills among different stakeholders in Bangladesh, Kenya and Nepal for communicating effective WCIS
2: To enhance cross-disciplinary collaboration in the development of WCIS in Bangladesh, Kenya and Nepal and increase co-production with end users. 
3: To increase the accessibility, timeliness, relevance, usefulness of, and trust in, weather and climate information services in Bangladesh, Kenya and Nepal
4: To increase global interest and knowledge relating to integration of effective communication approaches and WCIS</narrative>
  </description>
